    {
      "id": "CO-ING-8-2026-W18-gerunds-infinitives-001-MASTERY-v1",
      "statement": "I really enjoy ________ to vallenato music during the weekends.",
      "context": "Verbs of preference.",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "to listen",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrect. \"Enjoy\" is followed by -ing."
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "listening",
          "is_correct": true,
          "feedback": "Correct! After \"enjoy\", we must use the gerund (-ing)."
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "listen",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrect."
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "listened",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrect."
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": "B",
      "explanation": "En inglés, ciertos verbos como \"enjoy\", \"finish\" y \"mind\" siempre van seguidos de un gerundio (forma -ing).\n\n---",
