    {
      "id": "CO-ING-8-2026-W18-gerunds-infinitives-001-MASTERY-v5",
      "statement": "I stopped ________ bread because I'm on a diet. (I don't eat bread anymore).",
      "context": "Verbs followed by either form with different meanings.",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "to eat",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrect. \"Stop to eat\" means you paused another activity to eat."
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "eating",
          "is_correct": true,
          "feedback": "Correct! \"Stop + gerund\" means to quit or finish an activity."
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "eat",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrect."
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "ate",
          "is_correct": false,
          "feedback": "Incorrect."
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": "B",
      "explanation": "Algunos verbos como \"stop\" cambian su significado según lo que les siga. \"Stop eating\" significa dejar de comer algo permanentemente; \"Stop to eat\" significa detenerse un momento para comer algo.\n\n---",
